WEBVTT

00:09.050 --> 00:11.060
We'll be heading south of Mismede,

00:11.060 --> 00:15.480
past the Sea of Trees to the 
Burning Kingdom of Sandora,

00:15.480 --> 00:17.660
and then to the Rabbi Desert 
southeast of there!

00:18.420 --> 00:20.990
I heard that long ago, 
there were six stone pillars

00:20.990 --> 00:24.660
embedded with spellstones lying 
within ancient ruins in that desert!

00:25.180 --> 00:28.940
Though apparently those ruins have 
now been swallowed up by the desert.

00:30.070 --> 00:30.880
Good for you.

00:30.880 --> 00:34.310
What's with that completely 
disinterested reaction?

00:34.310 --> 00:36.380
You're not thinking you can 
just go poke your head in,

00:36.380 --> 00:39.380
take a look, and come right back home, are you?

00:39.380 --> 00:40.600
How did you know?

00:40.600 --> 00:42.560
Naughty underwear.

00:42.560 --> 00:44.100
I get it, okay?!

00:44.100 --> 00:45.060
Underwear?

00:45.060 --> 00:47.090
What is she talking about?

00:47.090 --> 00:49.270
It's nothing! Nothing at all!

00:49.640 --> 00:52.050
I just hope it's the Library. Right?

00:52.050 --> 00:54.810
<i>I don't think we need to 
work that hard to find it...</i>

00:54.810 --> 00:57.620
<i>But I am curious about the extermination</i>

00:57.620 --> 01:00.490
<i>of an ancient civilization 
at the hands of the Phrase.</i>

01:01.080 --> 01:03.090
<i>It's all well and good if 
I'm just overthinking it,</i>

01:03.090 --> 01:07.720
<i>but there's a chance we may need the power 
of Babylon if the worst comes to pass,</i>

01:07.720 --> 01:11.170
<i>and I refuse to regret not 
acting before it's too late.</i>

01:11.170 --> 01:13.620
Master, look at that!

01:15.180 --> 01:16.280
A Phrase?!

01:21.260 --> 01:22.640
What do we do?

01:22.640 --> 01:24.980
We can't just leave them be.

02:58.030 --> 03:03.030
Chapter 2

02:58.030 --> 03:03.030
The Stranded and the Workshop

03:19.010 --> 03:20.590
This way, while you can!

03:22.150 --> 03:23.480
Hide behind here.

03:23.480 --> 03:25.200
Wh-Who are you?

03:25.200 --> 03:26.260
Touya-dono!

03:26.260 --> 03:28.430
Send me above it with Gate!

03:30.780 --> 03:31.560
Got it!

03:35.370 --> 03:37.610
Prepare yourself!

03:39.190 --> 03:40.440
It didn't work?

03:41.540 --> 03:42.360
Yae?!

03:42.360 --> 03:44.240
Touya-dono! Use Gate!

03:47.060 --> 03:48.450
My apologies.

03:50.740 --> 03:51.910
Everyone, spread out!

03:57.980 --> 03:59.500
You've got to be kidding me!

03:59.500 --> 04:01.800
We'd be goners if we took a blow from that.

04:02.170 --> 04:04.280
I wondered who it was. It's you, Touya?

04:05.450 --> 04:06.500
Ende?!

04:08.360 --> 04:10.490
Hey, long time no see.

04:10.490 --> 04:12.930
I sensed the Phrase and came out here,

04:12.930 --> 04:14.980
but I didn't expect to run into you.

04:15.370 --> 04:17.980
You know about the Phrase?

04:17.980 --> 04:19.360
I do.

04:20.190 --> 04:24.030
Though I'm surprised a Standard 
Phrase has made it this far.

04:24.030 --> 04:26.990
I guess the World Barrier 
is already at its limit.

04:26.990 --> 04:27.660
Huh?

04:27.660 --> 04:29.920
Anyway, hang on a sec.

04:29.920 --> 04:31.950
I'll take care of that first.

04:34.190 --> 04:35.290
Hup.

04:41.460 --> 04:42.680
What?!

04:50.940 --> 04:52.920
What the heck did you do?

04:52.920 --> 04:53.940
Nothing.

04:54.330 --> 04:58.810
I just destroyed it by hitting it with 
magic attuned to its natural frequency.

04:58.810 --> 05:00.040
Ende...

05:00.040 --> 05:02.990
You just mentioned a "World Barrier," right?

05:02.990 --> 05:04.280
What is that?

05:04.680 --> 05:08.810
It's basically a net that keeps 
foreign things out of this world.

05:08.810 --> 05:11.490
Though it looks like it's starting to fray.

05:11.960 --> 05:14.250
This thing probably slipped through it, too.

05:14.250 --> 05:18.820
Though it's just a minion that 
only acts to achieve its goal.

05:18.820 --> 05:19.960
Goal?

05:19.960 --> 05:22.990
To find the Phrase's sleeping king.

05:22.990 --> 05:24.720
It's the same goal I have.

05:26.350 --> 05:27.940
I need to get going now.

05:27.940 --> 05:30.820
Farewell, Touya. I hope we meet again.

05:30.820 --> 05:31.640
Hey!

05:32.270 --> 05:34.100
The Phrase's king?

05:41.910 --> 05:43.320
That hits the spot.

05:43.850 --> 05:46.090
Touya, you have my gratitude.

05:46.090 --> 05:47.660
You saved us.

05:47.660 --> 05:50.430
I'm Rebecca, an adventurer.

05:50.430 --> 05:51.780
An adventurer?

05:51.780 --> 05:55.130
You all seem awfully lightly 
armed for adventurers.

05:55.130 --> 05:57.750
Those girls aren't adventurers.

05:57.750 --> 06:01.210
The things around their necks 
are Enslavement Collars.

06:01.210 --> 06:03.110
Enslavement Collars?

06:03.110 --> 06:05.090
Once it's on you, that's it.

06:05.090 --> 06:06.960
It's a magic item that makes 
you unable to defy orders,

06:06.960 --> 06:08.520
even when you're treated as property.

06:08.520 --> 06:11.070
Attempting to remove it 
will inflict intense pain

06:11.070 --> 06:13.310
that can lead to death at its worst.

06:13.310 --> 06:14.950
That's awful.

06:14.950 --> 06:18.050
Yeah, it's truly cruel.

06:18.050 --> 06:21.010
Only the person who placed 
it on them can remove it,

06:21.010 --> 06:23.520
but that person is already dead.

06:23.520 --> 06:25.370
Once we heard about their situation,

06:25.370 --> 06:28.760
we decided to help them flee the country.

06:28.760 --> 06:33.360
We thought we might be able to find a way
to remove the collars somewhere else.

06:33.360 --> 06:36.340
Anyway, pathetic as it is, 
we got lost and stranded,

06:36.340 --> 06:39.500
and then that monster attacked us, too.

06:39.500 --> 06:40.920
Hey, Touya.

06:41.410 --> 06:44.110
I think I might be able to 
remove those collars.

06:44.110 --> 06:45.250
What?!

06:49.880 --> 06:50.880
Apport.

06:52.510 --> 06:54.970
Th-The collar is off!

06:54.970 --> 06:59.570
Apport! Apport! Apport! 
Apport! Apport! Apport!

07:00.920 --> 07:02.690
What are you going to do now?

07:02.690 --> 07:07.590
Removing the collars still 
doesn't wipe their records.

07:07.590 --> 07:10.490
Staying in Sandora would 
bring them nothing but trouble.

07:10.490 --> 07:14.070
So we're still planning to take 
them to some other nation...

07:14.070 --> 07:17.230
In that case, would you like to go to Belfast?

07:17.230 --> 07:17.870
Huh?

07:17.870 --> 07:18.830
Who are you?

07:18.830 --> 07:20.500
Nice to meet you.

07:20.500 --> 07:25.060
I am Yumina Urnea Belfast, 
daughter of Tristwyn Urnes Belfast,

07:25.060 --> 07:27.840
King of the Kingdom of Belfast.

07:27.840 --> 07:28.580
Huh?!

07:28.580 --> 07:31.180
I heard everything about your situation.

07:31.680 --> 07:35.040
My country would be able to take you in.

07:35.040 --> 07:36.680
Would you like to come?

07:38.460 --> 07:42.310
U-Um, p-please, if we can!

07:44.810 --> 07:47.180
Then let's send everyone to Belfast.

07:47.630 --> 07:49.780
Touya, if you would?

07:52.200 --> 07:53.440
There.

07:59.980 --> 08:03.400
Rebecca-san and the others can 
live in my house for a while,

08:03.400 --> 08:06.500
and figure out what their 
future looks like later.

08:06.500 --> 08:09.710
Now, shall we continue on to the ruins?

08:09.710 --> 08:10.950
Before we do that...

08:11.790 --> 08:13.860
Who was that boy earlier?

08:13.860 --> 08:15.390
What's your relationship?

08:15.390 --> 08:18.990
O-Oh, right.

08:18.990 --> 08:22.250
Uh, his name is Ende,

08:22.250 --> 08:25.850
and I met him when I went to 
buy everyone's engagement rings.

08:26.880 --> 08:28.210
He was trying to buy some things

08:28.210 --> 08:31.120
with a strange coin he claimed 
he used to be able to use,

08:31.120 --> 08:35.560
but the shopkeeper rejected 
the coin, so I paid for him.

08:36.350 --> 08:39.620
He said he wanted to work since 
he'd be in trouble without money,

08:39.620 --> 08:41.620
so I led him to the guild.

08:41.620 --> 08:43.900
I managed to register, thanks to your help.

08:43.900 --> 08:45.220
Thank you, Touya.

08:45.720 --> 08:47.850
I hope we meet again somewhere.

08:49.660 --> 08:53.940
I never thought we'd meet again 
in the middle of the desert, though.

08:56.010 --> 08:59.460
The currency from here is still being used?

08:59.460 --> 09:02.130
Cesca, you recognize this money?

09:02.130 --> 09:03.580
I'm shocked.

09:04.140 --> 09:06.270
That is a Partheno silver coin.

09:06.270 --> 09:10.620
It was first minted 5,284 years ago.

09:10.620 --> 09:11.670
Huh?!

09:11.670 --> 09:15.820
It doesn't look like such a long 
time has passed for this coin.

09:17.280 --> 09:20.000
So he possessed a 5,000-year-old coin,

09:20.000 --> 09:23.820
and defeated a monster we 
couldn't scratch in a single blow.

09:23.820 --> 09:26.580
He also knew about that monster in detail,

09:26.580 --> 09:29.270
and wore a muffler even in this heat.

09:29.270 --> 09:31.250
He's just bursting with suspiciousness.

09:31.250 --> 09:34.210
I don't think that last one 
has much to do with anything,

09:34.210 --> 09:36.670
but I guess the fact remains 
that he is suspicious.

09:37.100 --> 09:38.220
<i>Ende...</i>

09:38.220 --> 09:40.240
<i>Just who is he, then?</i>

09:40.720 --> 09:43.760
Hey, that crystalline monster...

09:43.760 --> 09:45.880
He called it a Phrase, right?

09:45.880 --> 09:47.850
What exactly was that?

09:48.970 --> 09:51.640
You know something, don't you, Touya?

09:52.770 --> 09:56.290
Actually, I received a message 
from the professor.

09:56.290 --> 10:00.030
The same Professor Regina Babylon 
that created this Garden and Cesca.

10:00.820 --> 10:04.520
Apparently, the professor was using 
a device to look into the future,

10:04.520 --> 10:07.250
and observing our lives from the past.

10:07.810 --> 10:08.700
But then,

10:09.210 --> 10:15.630
one day, the Phrase suddenly appeared 
out of nowhere, and Partheno collapsed.

10:15.630 --> 10:18.180
The professor said she was 
able to predict the events

10:18.180 --> 10:21.930
leading to the world's 
destruction by the Phrase,

10:22.440 --> 10:25.320
but for some reason, 
the world wasn't destroyed.

10:25.320 --> 10:31.050
She had no idea why, but at a certain point, 
the Phrase just disappeared from this world.

10:31.900 --> 10:33.380
What?

10:33.380 --> 10:36.120
Why did you keep something 
that important from us?

10:36.120 --> 10:40.160
Well, I was planning to tell all 
of you about it eventually...

10:40.160 --> 10:42.720
An invasion of thousands of Phrases...

10:42.720 --> 10:46.050
So that's what wiped out 
the ancient civilization.

10:46.050 --> 10:50.190
Though, despite there being so 
many of them 5,000 years ago,

10:50.190 --> 10:52.630
there's hardly any eyewitness 
information about them in this era.

10:53.100 --> 10:55.520
Yet now they have begun appearing again.

10:55.520 --> 10:58.130
What exactly is going on?

10:58.480 --> 11:00.240
Ende did say that

11:00.240 --> 11:04.390
the barrier that keeps foreign things 
from entering this world was fraying,

11:04.990 --> 11:08.650
and that the Phrase from earlier 
had probably slipped through there.

11:10.210 --> 11:11.450
Cesca.

11:11.450 --> 11:15.470
Did mankind not fight 
the Phrase 5,000 years ago?

11:15.470 --> 11:19.820
No, the battles were rather dire, 
but they did fight back.

11:19.820 --> 11:24.460
The professor even developed decisive 
weapons for use against the Phrase,

11:24.460 --> 11:29.150
but by the time they were complete, 
there wasn't a single Phrase left.

11:29.150 --> 11:30.290
Decisive weapons?

11:30.290 --> 11:35.630
The professor created Frame Gears, 
pilotable humanoid combat weapons.

11:35.980 --> 11:38.660
Pilotable humanoid combat weapons?!

11:38.660 --> 11:42.100
The professor created things like that, too?!

11:42.100 --> 11:44.090
What happened to them after that?

11:44.090 --> 11:47.680
If I recall correctly, they were 
stored in the Hangar of Babylon.

11:47.680 --> 11:51.680
Which means that if the ruins we're 
heading toward teleport us to the Hangar,

11:51.680 --> 11:54.230
we'll be able to obtain them?!

11:54.230 --> 11:55.060
Yes.

11:55.570 --> 11:57.250
Huh? Oh, man!

11:57.250 --> 12:00.610
I'm getting a little... no, <i>really</i> excited!

12:00.610 --> 12:03.530
Master, we've arrived at our destination.

12:06.310 --> 12:07.800
There's nothing here...

12:17.340 --> 12:21.380
Whirl forth, Wind! A Tempestuous 
Whirlwind, Cyclone Storm!

12:31.120 --> 12:33.300
It was buried in a place like this?

12:34.790 --> 12:36.730
How do we get this open?

12:38.060 --> 12:39.400
Touya!

12:39.400 --> 12:40.650
Whoa!

12:45.250 --> 12:46.230
Gate.

12:46.820 --> 12:49.840
Huh? My magic isn't activating?

12:50.360 --> 12:52.010
Am I trapped in here?

12:52.540 --> 12:54.750
Are you okay, Master?!

12:54.750 --> 12:55.870
Kohaku?

12:55.870 --> 12:58.290
Yeah, I'm fine. It was harmless.

12:58.980 --> 13:00.880
There's a teleportation circle inside.

13:00.880 --> 13:04.560
I'm going to try going in, so tell 
everyone not to worry about me.

13:04.560 --> 13:07.260
All right. Be careful.

13:09.450 --> 13:12.600
I guess I can't get out unless 
I use the teleportation circle.

13:24.110 --> 13:25.150
Okay.

13:25.470 --> 13:27.240
I hope it's the Hangar.

13:38.810 --> 13:40.540
Stop right there!

13:45.880 --> 13:48.390
Welcome to the Workshop of Babylon.

13:48.390 --> 13:52.300
I am the administration terminal 
for this place, High Rosetta.

13:52.300 --> 13:55.350
I would be grateful if 
you would call me Rosetta.

13:55.350 --> 13:58.060
The Workshop, huh?

13:58.060 --> 14:01.170
The hub of the Workshop is up ahead.

14:01.470 --> 14:05.780
Currently, entry is forbidden 
to all but the compatible one.

14:05.780 --> 14:10.120
Well, I have been deemed 
compatible by Cesca.

14:10.580 --> 14:11.930
Cesca?

14:11.930 --> 14:14.100
You mean Francesca?

14:14.100 --> 14:18.180
I see. So you have already 
obtained the Garden.

14:18.180 --> 14:20.330
That will make this much quicker.

14:20.330 --> 14:25.340
I will now test you to determine if you 
are qualified to be the compatible one!

14:25.340 --> 14:28.040
Test me? What are you going to do?

14:28.550 --> 14:33.180
Guess the color of my panties 
without moving a step from there!

14:33.180 --> 14:34.680
You moron!

14:34.680 --> 14:37.330
Seriously, what was that professor thinking?!

14:37.330 --> 14:40.850
Hey, what did I tell you? 
You can't move from there.

14:40.850 --> 14:43.610
What, then? Are you telling 
me to flip up your skirt?

14:43.610 --> 14:44.440
You moron!

14:44.440 --> 14:48.840
If you can pull it off without moving 
from there, that would also be fine!

14:48.840 --> 14:51.150
However, you can only answer once!

14:51.150 --> 14:53.030
Your time limit is five minutes!

14:53.030 --> 14:55.900
Why are you so into this?!

14:55.900 --> 14:58.640
Go on, what color are they?

14:58.640 --> 15:02.000
I hate playing into your hands 
like this, but I'll do it!

15:02.390 --> 15:06.210
Blow forth, Wind! Rising 
Whirlwind, Cool Wind!

15:14.770 --> 15:16.720
Wh-What?!

15:16.720 --> 15:20.350
This skirt turns away Wind magic.

15:20.350 --> 15:21.580
In that case...

15:21.580 --> 15:25.780
Burn forth, Fire! Breath 
of Flame, Fire Breath!

15:30.320 --> 15:31.530
What?!

15:31.530 --> 15:34.990
It also turns away Fire magic, 
just as it does Wind.

15:34.990 --> 15:37.390
What's with that ultimate skirt?!

15:37.390 --> 15:39.480
It's uselessly high-spec!

15:39.480 --> 15:41.130
Don't go getting cocky, though.

15:41.130 --> 15:44.960
If you make me get serious, I can 
peek at your panties whenever I want!

15:45.330 --> 15:49.620
<i>At this point, I'll just send my vision 
under her skirt and peek at them directly!</i>

15:50.320 --> 15:51.340
Long Sense!

15:57.050 --> 15:59.430
Now, what color are they?

16:00.900 --> 16:03.690
Colorless... Transparent...

16:03.690 --> 16:05.750
That's correct!

16:05.750 --> 16:07.670
I now recognize you as compatible,

16:07.670 --> 16:12.010
and as of this moment, Unit #27, 
code name "High Rosetta,"

16:12.010 --> 16:14.450
will be transferred to your command!

16:14.930 --> 16:17.670
Master, are you all right?

16:17.670 --> 16:19.950
Y-Yeah...

16:19.950 --> 16:22.910
Is that so? Moving on, then.

16:24.750 --> 16:25.380
Huh?

16:29.230 --> 16:30.540
Registration complete.

16:30.540 --> 16:32.860
Genetic information recorded.

16:32.860 --> 16:36.800
Ownership of the Workshop 
is now transferred to Master.

16:37.300 --> 16:40.350
<i>Oh, for crying out loud... I'll get her for this.</i>

16:43.120 --> 16:46.020
Are you truly all right now?

16:46.020 --> 16:47.020
Yeah.

16:47.020 --> 16:49.910
Then I shall show you the Workshop.

16:56.730 --> 17:01.890
Is this whole building just 
an assembly of tiny cubes?

17:06.260 --> 17:07.810
What is this?

17:08.590 --> 17:10.770
This is the Workshop.

17:15.050 --> 17:19.950
It is an all-purpose factory that can create
any manufacturing apparatus you imagine,

17:19.950 --> 17:23.930
and any work spaces needed 
to support production.

17:23.930 --> 17:25.370
I see.

17:25.370 --> 17:29.350
So it can manipulate the minuscule 
blocks that compose this very building

17:29.350 --> 17:32.820
into any manner of tool or device?

17:32.820 --> 17:37.240
The only ones able to manipulate the 
Workshop are myself and you, Master.

17:37.240 --> 17:40.190
Also, if you have a product 
to serve as the original,

17:40.190 --> 17:42.820
it's possible to reproduce it here.

17:42.820 --> 17:47.080
Provided that you have all the 
component materials, of course.

17:48.170 --> 17:53.660
I wouldn't have much need of this place 
since I can make things with Modeling,

17:53.660 --> 17:57.630
but it's a different story if it 
can mass-produce what I make.

17:58.680 --> 18:00.470
Can you reproduce this?

18:00.470 --> 18:01.630
For the materials...

18:03.470 --> 18:04.730
Use mythril.

18:04.730 --> 18:06.360
Of course.

18:07.810 --> 18:09.230
Scan.

18:11.770 --> 18:13.260
Copy.

18:18.660 --> 18:19.780
It's fast!

18:20.630 --> 18:22.540
You can also do this...

18:26.800 --> 18:30.540
to freely alter the design.

18:38.030 --> 18:39.180
Blade Mode.

18:40.290 --> 18:43.140
I guess it can't copy Program along with it.

18:43.520 --> 18:46.330
Well, that just means I need 
to reinstate Program on it.

18:46.330 --> 18:48.760
If you will a certain number to be copied,

18:48.760 --> 18:51.520
it will continue production automatically.

18:51.520 --> 18:53.800
I see. That's convenient.

18:53.800 --> 18:55.190
This can earn money.

18:55.190 --> 18:59.320
Though this makes it more 
of a factory than a workshop.

18:59.990 --> 19:01.720
Oh, yeah! Rosetta,

19:01.720 --> 19:06.810
there was something created to fight 
the Phrase, right? Cesca mentioned it.

19:06.810 --> 19:09.180
You mean the Frame Gears, yes?

19:09.180 --> 19:12.180
Those certainly were created here.

19:12.180 --> 19:15.090
I helped the professor build them.

19:15.090 --> 19:16.730
I knew it.

19:17.310 --> 19:18.930
<i>So they were developed in the Workshop,</i>

19:18.930 --> 19:22.780
<i>and the completed ones were 
later stored in the Hangar?</i>

19:22.780 --> 19:25.430
<i>She could have just left them here...</i>

19:25.890 --> 19:28.630
Rosetta, can you create those Frame Gears?

19:28.630 --> 19:30.730
That's impossible for me.

19:30.730 --> 19:31.470
Huh?

19:31.470 --> 19:35.080
At present, the most I can 
create is their equipment.

19:35.080 --> 19:37.150
I don't have their blueprints.

19:37.150 --> 19:40.070
Though the blueprints 
might be in the Storehouse.

19:40.070 --> 19:41.800
I see.

19:41.800 --> 19:43.570
Then we either need to find the Hangar,

19:43.570 --> 19:46.600
or find the Storehouse and 
have Rosetta build them.

19:46.600 --> 19:49.720
Either way, there's nothing 
we can do at present.

19:49.720 --> 19:51.690
I guess I'll get everyone here for now.

19:51.690 --> 19:54.190
Cesca probably wants to see you, too.

19:54.190 --> 19:56.590
Great! I'm looking forward to it!

19:59.450 --> 20:00.560
And there!

20:01.590 --> 20:03.630
The Workshop, huh?

20:03.630 --> 20:05.930
That makes me kind of irritated.

20:06.420 --> 20:10.550
This is far more useful than the Garden, 
which serves no purpose on its own.

20:10.550 --> 20:11.470
Excuse me.

20:11.470 --> 20:13.860
My Garden has been Master's mental support

20:13.860 --> 20:18.400
by being a healing garden that provides 
peace of mind and a space to refresh.

20:18.400 --> 20:20.190
Your misconception is severe.

20:20.190 --> 20:22.070
Setting that aside!

20:22.070 --> 20:25.050
Is it possible to rejoin the
 Garden and the Workshop?

20:25.050 --> 20:28.610
Yes. Now that ownership has 
been transferred to Master,

20:28.610 --> 20:30.350
I believe that would be for the best.

20:30.350 --> 20:35.200
I've lowered the strength of the barrier, 
so it will be possible to link with the Garden.

20:35.200 --> 20:38.130
We can control the Garden from here, as well.

20:38.130 --> 20:41.130
What shall we do, Master?

20:41.130 --> 20:43.960
Have the Garden return to Belfast.

20:43.960 --> 20:46.700
Then have the Workshop 
head to Belfast, as well.

20:46.700 --> 20:48.500
We'll do the docking there.

20:48.500 --> 20:49.960
Docking...

20:50.480 --> 20:51.350
Huh?

20:51.850 --> 20:53.380
Sounds naughty.

20:53.380 --> 20:55.220
Just go do it already!

20:56.250 --> 20:58.060
My sincere apologies!

20:58.480 --> 21:03.280
I was unaware you were engaged to the 
princess! Please have mercy upon me!

21:03.280 --> 21:06.780
Hey, stop, stop! You're taking it too far!

21:06.780 --> 21:08.560
No, no, no!

21:08.560 --> 21:12.950
Cecile has told me what 
a wonderful man you are.

21:13.470 --> 21:16.130
Cecile-san, you said something 
you shouldn't have, didn't you?

21:16.960 --> 21:19.950
At any rate, please don't 
worry about it so much.

21:19.950 --> 21:23.390
Also, I'm not exactly a noble,

21:23.390 --> 21:26.050
so you don't have to force yourself 
to speak so politely, okay?

21:26.050 --> 21:27.520
Really?

21:27.520 --> 21:29.250
Then I'll take you up on that.

21:29.250 --> 21:31.500
Hey, now, are you sure?

21:31.500 --> 21:34.890
He said so himself. It should be fine.

21:34.890 --> 21:37.540
So what will you all do from now on?

21:37.540 --> 21:41.410
I imagine the three of you can earn 
a living working for the guild, but...

21:41.410 --> 21:43.230
You mean the girls, right?

21:45.950 --> 21:49.160
They don't have any special skills,

21:49.160 --> 21:51.620
and they can't exactly fight, either.

21:53.110 --> 21:55.790
Would you be willing to let them stay here

21:55.790 --> 21:57.790
until they find work in this city?

21:57.790 --> 22:00.550
Sure, that part is fine.

22:00.550 --> 22:02.550
But work, huh?

22:02.550 --> 22:04.820
<i>Could I have them mass-produce 
something at the Workshop?</i>

22:04.820 --> 22:07.960
<i>No, I want to keep the Workshop a secret,</i>

22:07.960 --> 22:11.660
<i>and it would be better to ask a 
professional if I'm trading something.</i>

22:11.660 --> 22:14.040
<i>So they need some other kind of work...</i>

22:16.030 --> 22:18.930
<i>What should I do, I wonder?</i>
